(:screening :id "CARD-LAB" :date "2026-11-13" :model "vcGlm53Flash" :served "zai/glm-5.3-flash" :status "screening, n=1 per task, stopped at 67 of 120 trials; nothing here is a confirmed result" :src ("asl/bench/gen/cardLab/results/glm.asn first 62 rows" "asl/bench/gen/results/2026-11-13/glm.asn arm asl, 20 rows at 22:15") :method "raw pass = first reply regraded by asl/bench/gen/cardLab/regrade.asl with the graded cases; a row is valid when its first reply names the task's entry function" :spentUsd "0.17 at 62 rows, cap 1.0")
(:defect :id crossWiredReplies :sev high :where "asl/bench/gen/run.asl liveOnce! over gs/linkSend!" :seen "a trial row holds the solution of another task (row lookupChain holds trafficLightNext, row clampInt holds romanNumeral); 18 of 143 replies in the screening file from row 31 on, 13 of 327 in results/2026-11-13/glm.asn from row 121 on, 10 of 163 in ds.shard1.asn, 1 in ds.shard0.asn, 0 of 256 in haiku.asn" :hypothesis "after a call passes the 300 s link limit its late response is read as the reply to the next request, and the shift persists; not proven, the link code was not read" :effect "rows after the first shift are graded against the wrong task; the screening run was stopped by its writer for this reason and the running pilots carry the same rows")
(:defect :id rebuildTimeout :sev medium :where "gc/runAslFile! check step" :seen "while the shared native CLI is rebuilt a correct candidate is recorded as stage check four times in about 200 s; 4 of 62 screening rows pass on regrade though recorded failed" :effect "solved and tokens-to-green of such rows are unusable")
