(:reading :do "ASL is read as accurately as Python and TypeScript on result prediction (58 to 60 of 60, all arms within 2 items) but at 1.19 times the program tokens of Python and 1.4 to 2.3 times the output tokens. It loses on fixing: without a card 2 of the 3 wrong fixes write == for =, the same prior as in writing, and the third breaks a nested listAppend line; the wrong predictions of every arm are notation slips (a missing quote, text after the answer), not misread semantics. 14 bug items per arm is too few to separate 13 from 14")
